1
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Naka River,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,940
kicking a pebble, I fly off in a rush,

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,360
to Kashiwa,
the type who was always joking around,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,820
they laughed at me for
staying just as full of energy.

5
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:38,680
Even if I rouse my spirits somewhere,
I can only win.

6
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:43,900
One nightmare, but the unchanging
streetscape is kinder to me.

7
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:49,040
The crows are cawing,
so the day is already fading.

8
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:54,620
Watching the yakitori lanterns glow,
too, right?

9
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:59,380
From the acorn-shaped star,
from the first waterworks,

10
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:04,080
toward the vast sky, the sun sets.

11
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow, too,
it sinks and it all ends, doesn't it.

12
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,740
Katsushika, Shibamata,
they say happiness is here too.

13
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:14,640
I only realized it once I'd lost it.

14
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm such a fool.

15
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:28,080
Let's spread the circle of
police boxes across the world.

16
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:32,500
Kei-chan, that hair is lovely.

17
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:34,000
Do you understand?

18
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:35,560
It's Monsieur François.

19
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:37,520
Monsieur? François?

20
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:41,600
Yes, he's a hair and makeup artist,
a friend of mine who lives in Paris.

21
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:45,060
His staff opened a shop in Roppongi,

22
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:47,480
so he came to Japan
for the opening ceremony.

23
00:01:48,380 --> 00:01:51,180
I was invited too,
and I had the latest spring cut.

24
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:53,660
How do you like it?

25
00:01:54,620 --> 00:01:58,080
Natural and springlike,
just as expected from a Scissors Champion!

26
00:01:58,520 --> 00:01:59,640
Honda, do you get it?

27
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:02,620
Well, it looks the same as usual to me.

28
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:06,460
It's the same as always. As long as there's hair on your head,
that's all that matters.

29
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:09,360
No matter how much a man fusses over his looks,
it's no use.

30
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:13,940
Nakagawa-san! Nakagawa-san, you're so cool!
Please sign this!

31
00:02:13,940 --> 00:02:19,240
Shut up! A signature?
Nakagawa isn't an idol, for crying out loud!

32
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:23,560
Damn it, it was almost finished,
and now I have to start over again!

33
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:28,080
Reiko-san also goes all the way to
London to get her haircut, right?

34
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,340
Yes, from Mrs. Elizabeth.

35
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:34,040
What, you go overseas just to get a haircut?

36
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:36,560
Rich people really are different.

37
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:43,320
When I was a newly minted officer, I often flew back
and forth overseas on the Concorde for haircuts too.

38
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,240
Kankara!

39
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:50,640
During my training period, when I couldn't get time off,
I had my hairstylist fly to Japan on a chartered plane.

40
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:52,220
Chartered plane.

41
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:57,220
What's with this charter plane nonsense?

42
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:59,600
Wasting money on your hair like that.

43
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,740
Hairstyles don't matter at all.

44
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:04,200
See, a charter plane.

45
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:11,080
Still, a hairstyle is a big factor
in how people see you, right?

46
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:14,120
Speaking of which, Senpai,
you always have a crew cut.

47
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:16,680
Isn't there some particular reason for it?

48
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:21,000
My crew cut is just
because it's easy to order.

49
00:03:23,220 --> 00:03:29,360
When I need to, I zip around on my bike wherever I please.
Not fussing over hair is my policy.

50
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:39,060
That's it, Senpai, maybe that shop could cut your hair.
There's a barbershop in Fukagawa that specializes, or rather focuses only on crew cuts.

51
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:40,776
Crew cuts only?

52
00:03:40,826 --> 00:03:46,660
Well, the owner there is a bit odd,
or rather, difficult to deal with.

53
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:52,760
Customers he doesn't like get thrown out of the shop left and right,
and they can't get a haircut.

54
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:54,680
What's that supposed to mean?

55
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:59,920
But I hear he doesn't charge
the customers he really likes.

56
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:00,980
Is that true?

57
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:04,680
Sounds right up your alley, Ryo-chan,
an old-school craftsman from the old town.

58
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:08,880
Maybe barbershops like that
will come back into fashion.

59
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:10,640
Maybe crew cuts will become popular too.

60
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:15,140
In Fukagawa, the word is that
a crew-cut boom is about to hit.

61
00:04:16,660 --> 00:04:17,160
Honda

62
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:25,380
That shop's guy is definitely
going to be trouble, right?

63
00:04:25,380 --> 00:04:26,300
Hey,

64
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:32,800
other than the sign, that barbershop nearby
is just an ordinary barbershop, right?

65
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:34,540
The old man is scary.

66
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:36,140
This damn crew cut!

67
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:36,260
2

68
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:37,180
Same.

69
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:39,840
One more.

70
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:44,200
Don't you ever touch anyone's
head with those hands again!

71
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,660
Drop dead, you crew-cut old geezer!

72
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:46,360
What?!

73
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:47,680
Say that again!

74
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:50,660
Yeah, I'll say it as many times as you want!
Crew-cut old geezer!

75
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:53,100
Screw you!

76
00:04:55,460 --> 00:04:56,500
That idiot.

77
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:57,800
I see.

78
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:02,400
So, what do I have to do to get on
that stubborn old man's good side?

79
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:06,140
I'm not a crew cut guy,
so I've never actually been inside the shop.

80
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:08,040
Besides, I'm no good with scary people.

81
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,240
What?

82
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:12,900
Whatever. Since we're getting free haircuts,
we don't need any smiles.

83
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:16,040
Old men are my specialty.

84
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:17,860
Senpai, please be careful.

85
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:22,200
If I don't make it back alive,

86
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:24,520
then Kameari is in your hands.

87
00:05:25,070 --> 00:05:26,180
Right, Senpai?

88
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:29,980
Don't think I've seen your face around.

89
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:33,780
Hey, who the hell are you with?

90
00:05:33,780 --> 00:05:35,840
Yikes, that's scary.

91
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:39,200
In a game of chance,
the start is what counts.

92
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:44,460
Hold on, let me introduce myself properly.

93
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:47,220
Born in Asakusa, my name is Kankichi Ryotsu.

94
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:48,660
I'm a stingy bastard.

95
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:50,540
These days I live in Kameari.

96
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:53,120
Shibamata.

97
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:56,380
You know this is a
crew-cut-only shop, right?

98
00:05:56,380 --> 00:05:58,380
Ever since I came wailing into this world,

99
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:00,060
haircuts other than the crew cut

100
00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:02,620
I've never tried them,
I'm just a clumsy guy.

101
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:15,960
Wait over there.

102
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:20,740
Yay, as expected of senpai, breezing
right through the first checkpoint too!

103
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:38,200
The models are all scary-looking guys.

104
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:40,140
The crew cut suits you.

105
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:42,180
Even the sign outside,

106
00:06:42,180 --> 00:06:44,340
the creams and hair tonics too,

107
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:46,360
even the decorative kokeshi dolls,

108
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:48,640
everything here is so squared off.

109
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:50,520
It really is a crew-cut palace, isn't it.

110
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:51,440
Done.

111
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:53,500
No reversal this time either

112
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,100
Too bad, though.

113
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:56,440
Reversal?

114
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:56,940
Next.

115
00:06:56,940 --> 00:06:57,760
Yeah.

116
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:03,180
One crew cut, coming right up!

117
00:07:03,180 --> 00:07:03,560
Hup!

118
00:07:06,580 --> 00:07:09,500
Apparently there are all
sorts of rituals before the cut.

119
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:18,380
Clippers on the household shrine, check!
Yeaaah... what's this guy?

120
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:26,420
What now? Just as I thought, he's got a great face.
Coarse hair, thick eyebrows, and a thick neck too.

121
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:29,920
He's got a face that
was born for the crew cut.

122
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:32,320
Thanks.

123
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:36,180
I might be the first person ever
to get compliments on my face.

124
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:38,860
Feels like the owner
has taken a liking to me.

125
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:48,280
These days, every young man is a skinny,
lanky weakling.

126
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:51,760
Nothing but faces that don't suit a crew cut.
It's just no good.

127
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:53,440
It's exasperating.

128
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:55,420
Right, this one.

129
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:59,480
His jaw just won't develop.

130
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:05,960
No!

131
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:08,360
Don't move!

132
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:10,840
Here goes.

133
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:18,000
Man, this is worse than
torture during the qualifiers.

134
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:29,120
Yeah, yeah, yeah...

135
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:30,640
Uh

136
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:36,260
How's that?

137
00:08:36,260 --> 00:08:38,060
Don't I look more handsome now?

138
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:38,660
Good.

139
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:41,560
It's been on since before then.

140
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:43,760
I had a great time today.

141
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:45,740
Keep your money, I don't need it.

142
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:47,620
Just as I expected,
you wouldn't just let me go.

143
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:49,020
Sorry about that.

144
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:49,880
23

145
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:52,480
Didn't you hear this one?
Is it the reversal?

146
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:54,320
My dream is,

147
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:57,592
well, for every man in the world,

148
00:08:57,642 --> 00:09:00,300
to get a crew cut.

149
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:04,560
The whole world Sorry to keep you waiting.

150
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:08,180
Just as expected of you, senior.
You got the reversal in one shot.

151
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:09,920
What? Reversal?

152
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:10,700
No way?

153
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:11,740
That's incredible right off the bat.

154
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:12,980
What's with these guys?

155
00:09:13,060 --> 00:09:17,192
Since senior got the Barber Shibata
lifetime free pass reversal in one go,

156
00:09:17,242 --> 00:09:18,540
we're just jealous.

157
00:09:18,900 --> 00:09:21,160
What? A lifetime free pass?

158
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:24,200
So this thing comes with
such a valuable bonus point?

159
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:34,180
Who are those guys?

160
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:37,580
Ryo-san's hair is scary.

161
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:39,890
I've never been popular with women,

162
00:09:39,940 --> 00:09:43,480
but Ryo-san was the most
popular with the kids.

163
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,300
Is it because of this place after all?

164
00:09:45,380 --> 00:09:47,700
We'll just have to wait for it to grow back.

165
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:52,280
That Shibata place and its customers appeal to connoisseurs,
and they even hand out things like this,

166
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:54,480
so it's become a business

167
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:57,840
I hear the inside situation
is pretty tough, though.

168
00:09:57,840 --> 00:10:00,540
He really is a crew-cut idiot of an old man.

169
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:04,420
But if that barber
Shibata's business goes under,

170
00:10:04,420 --> 00:10:08,280
the free-pass perk is obviously out

171
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:10,940
That's a problem!

172
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:12,680
What's the problem, Ryo-chan?

173
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:14,260
N-nothing, never mind.

174
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:16,780
Reiko, that hair looks great on you.

175
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:21,220
I don't get it at all.

176
00:10:21,220 --> 00:10:24,580
It feels natural and
subtly reflects the times.

177
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:27,540
As expected of Mrs. Elizabeth,
the Scissors Queen.

178
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:31,620
Apparently the World Scissors Contest
is being held in Tokyo this weekend.

179
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:34,680
That's why she's suddenly coming to Japan,
they said.

180
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:38,360
I got a call earlier,
and she cut my hair during my lunch break.

181
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:43,440
Is Mrs. Elizabeth going to compete
in the World Scissors Contest?

182
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:44,520
That's right.

183
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:47,960
I've been asked to be
the hair model on the day.

184
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:52,240
Me too.
I got a call earlier from Monsieur François.

185
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:57,840
If Monsieur François enters the contest, it'll
be a head-to-head showdown with Mrs. Elizabeth.

186
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:58,680
Yeah, it will.

187
00:10:59,060 --> 00:11:01,740
What's this World Scissors Contest, then?

188
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:08,440
It's the world's largest haircut contest, where hairdressers
and barbers selected from all over the world gather in one place.

189
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:13,560
So it's being held in Tokyo.
Is there prize money?

190
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:17,680
If I remember right,
the winner gets 10 million yen.

191
00:11:19,060 --> 00:11:23,480
Honda, didn't you say crew cuts
were about to become popular?

192
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:26,060
It's already a rumor around Fukagawa.

193
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:30,100
If we persuade him that it's for
the spread and status of crew cuts,

194
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:34,760
My dream is for every man in
the world to get a crew cut.

195
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:37,560
That stubborn old man won't refuse, surely.

196
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:39,760
Could it be, senpai?

197
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:43,380
We're going to drag Barber
Shibata into the scissors contest.

198
00:11:57,960 --> 00:12:00,680
Contests aren't really my style.

199
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:04,080
Thanks for the offer, but I'm passing.

200
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:04,700
Just as I thought.

201
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:05,520
Why?

202
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,200
Why?

203
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:10,860
I'm not very good with my hands.

204
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:12,660
You're plenty skilled, though.

205
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:17,800
Just the other day you said your dream

206
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:19,620
was giving every man in the world a crew cut,
didn't you?

207
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:21,060
That's...

208
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:24,080
Your talent is wasted if you keep

209
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,820
being so picky about
customers like you were today.

210
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:26,940
Eventually it'll rust away.

211
00:12:28,060 --> 00:12:30,040
Then just get out, you stubborn old fool.

212
00:12:32,340 --> 00:12:33,260
The other day,

213
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:36,100
What the hell are you doing here,
you little brat?

214
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:37,820
I also, the other day,

215
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:40,580
told that stubborn head about the contest.

216
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:41,480
And then,

217
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:44,420
crew cuts only aren't in style these days,
you know.

218
00:12:44,420 --> 00:12:46,600
You should open your eyes to the world.

219
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:51,300
Don't you ever show that
shiny head of yours again!

220
00:12:51,300 --> 00:12:52,980
Drop dead, you crew-cut punk!

221
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:55,680
Even after being put through that,

222
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:57,660
Senpai, that look!

223
00:13:00,060 --> 00:13:02,660
Shibata,
are you two father and son or something?

224
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:06,760
Whatever you say, you're just
scared to leave Fukagawa, aren't you?

225
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:07,900
That's not true.

226
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:11,240
Then go and take the challenge.

227
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:13,180
Honda, that thing.

228
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:13,700
Yes.

229
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:18,720
The National Hairdressers Association also
readily wrote a letter of recommendation for you.

230
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:20,720
I went around to the local barbershops, and

231
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:24,900
they've all said they'll cheer
for you if Barber Shibata enters.

232
00:13:25,380 --> 00:13:27,120
Everyone's counting on you.

233
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:29,560
Let's take the world with crew cuts.

234
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:30,700
Dad.

235
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:36,160
Fine, but this time only.

236
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:36,900
Yay!

237
00:13:38,260 --> 00:13:41,000
So, we'll split the prize money, all right?

238
00:13:44,140 --> 00:13:46,220
I'm going in with only the crew cut.

239
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:51,120
But those places are flashy,
so won't a plain crew cut just blend in?

240
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:53,180
That's exactly where we'll aim.

241
00:13:53,180 --> 00:13:53,760
Honda.

242
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:54,100
Yes.

243
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:00,580
Simple is best.

244
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:05,560
Amid all this flashy, colorful scenery,
a plain black crew cut is sure to stand out.

245
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:09,360
It's less the hairstyle and more the sheer
force of the face that makes it stand out.

246
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Most of the contestants are foreigners, and from a
Tokyo novelty standpoint, the crew cut has the edge.

247
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:24,580
Each of those is totally unfunny. It's like the
crew cut can't win without a gimmick or local flavor.

248
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:32,260
That's not what I mean. What I'm saying is,
the crew cut is the best, period.

249
00:14:32,860 --> 00:14:34,840
But that's a problem.

250
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:36,020
What's the problem?

251
00:14:36,100 --> 00:14:39,080
Think of me as your corner
man and tell me anything.

252
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:41,040
To enter the contest,

253
00:14:41,040 --> 00:14:43,600
We need a model who suits a crew cut, but

254
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:45,400
I'm no good for that.

255
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:46,540
Don't worry.

256
00:14:46,540 --> 00:14:48,380
I'll be the model.

257
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:50,460
But the contest is on the weekend, right?

258
00:14:50,900 --> 00:14:52,160
You've got no hair, though.

259
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:54,640
Even I can't do a thing about that.

260
00:14:55,420 --> 00:14:56,800
No need to worry.

261
00:14:57,420 --> 00:14:57,800
What?

262
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:01,680
You'll need a hair-growth tonic.

263
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:02,828
This spring,

264
00:15:02,878 --> 00:15:08,600
I got my hands on Nakagawa Kemekaru's ultimate hair-growth tonic,
which they're launching in a big way, through some backroom dealing.

265
00:15:08,820 --> 00:15:11,401
Sprinkle this on the head,

266
00:15:11,451 --> 00:15:14,800
massage it in well, then wait a while.

267
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:17,640
Any moment now.

268
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:22,200
Good heavens.

269
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:23,900
You look like a caveman.

270
00:15:25,820 --> 00:15:27,340
Maybe I put on a bit too much.

271
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:31,240
Anyway, with a head that suits the
crew cut best in Japan as the cut model,

272
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:33,160
Barber Shibata's Japan champion

273
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:36,480
or rather,
with the world's best crew-cut technique,

274
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:37,880
victory is certain.

275
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:38,800
Right.

276
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:41,440
We've got an even more secret weapon.

277
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:44,020
But for now, I won't reveal it.

278
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:50,980
Let's go, Old Man Shibata.

279
00:15:50,980 --> 00:15:51,980
Yeah.

280
00:16:00,980 --> 00:16:02,220
Thank you for waiting.

281
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:05,620
The masters of the world's beauty industry,

282
00:16:05,620 --> 00:16:09,200
the day has come for them to compete for
the title of star in the scissors arena.

283
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:13,500
The winner will receive
a prize of 10 million yen

284
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:17,540
and these solid gold scissors
as an additional award.

285
00:16:19,060 --> 00:16:19,780
Yeah, that's it!

286
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:25,240
This event is being broadcast live
via satellite to the entire world.

287
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:29,840
World Scissors Contest 2004

288
00:16:30,640 --> 00:16:32,080
It's starting!

289
00:16:32,880 --> 00:16:35,300
And now,
the contestants will make their entrance.

290
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:42,250
It's Reiko,

291
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:46,900
good luck, Reiko!

292
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:49,000
The one who has to do the hard work is the hairdresser,
isn't it?

293
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:50,220
What's wrong with cheering?

294
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:52,080
Nakagawa's here too.

295
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:55,100
Hey, good luck, Nakagawa!

296
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:56,900
Look who's talking.

297
00:16:56,900 --> 00:16:58,440
A caveman spotted!

298
00:16:58,440 --> 00:17:00,500
W-what's with that hair?

299
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:02,400
He looks like a real caveman.

300
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:07,940
Looks like Shibata's really
nervous up on that unfamiliar stage.

301
00:17:07,940 --> 00:17:11,800
The others look like they're used to contests,
don't they?

302
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:14,200
He tripped.

303
00:17:14,600 --> 00:17:16,460
Old man, are you okay?

304
00:17:17,020 --> 00:17:20,760
He's just a little nervous since it's
his first time ever leaving Fukagawa.

305
00:17:21,260 --> 00:17:23,020
Once you start renting,
every place is the same.

306
00:17:23,380 --> 00:17:23,700
Alright.

307
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:28,220
The contest has a technical category,
judging precise and elegant scissor work,

308
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:32,640
and an artistic category, where each
contestant can fully display their originality.

309
00:17:32,980 --> 00:17:34,300
Originality?

310
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:37,140
Judging is done through
cuts in two categories,

311
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:42,000
and the top three contestants with the highest total
scores will be awarded the Scissors Master prize.

312
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:46,060
The judges are media
figures and fashion designers

313
00:17:46,460 --> 00:17:47,640
and critics from around the world.

314
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:51,360
And now, the technical category
of the first stage begins!

315
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:53,000
The time limit is 20 minutes.

316
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:54,820
Let's scissors!

317
00:17:54,820 --> 00:17:56,000
Good luck, old man!

318
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:57,260
Good luck, senior!

319
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:02,040
I can't breathe...

320
00:18:02,740 --> 00:18:03,780
S-sorry.

321
00:18:03,780 --> 00:18:05,720
It's fine, so calm down.

322
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:08,680
You just have to do your usual crew cut.

323
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:10,640
Leave the rest to me, got it?

324
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:11,640
R-right.

325
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:13,620
You don't have to worry.

326
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:19,140
The 10 million is as good as ours!

327
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:25,100
Your hair's grown!

328
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:02,780
We'll take first place next time
and the ten million yen is ours!

329
00:19:02,780 --> 00:19:03,400
Senpai

330
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:04,860
This is bad.

331
00:19:05,900 --> 00:19:06,680
What did you say?

332
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:10,680
You mixed Kei-chan's company's hair tonic into everyone's spray,
didn't you?

333
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:11,320
This.

334
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:12,960
What are they talking about?

335
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:16,140
What are you doing?

336
00:19:16,140 --> 00:19:17,440
I knew it.

337
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:21,680
The clearest proof is that during the contest,
all you wanted was for your senpai's hair to grow.

338
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:24,100
Do you have any proof that I did it?

339
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:27,260
At what exact hour, minute, and second?

340
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:31,680
Don't say that! Only Ryo-chan
would think of something like this!

341
00:19:31,860 --> 00:19:32,600
That's right!

342
00:19:33,100 --> 00:19:35,960
With that kind of setup, this won't be a fair contest!
Give up on winning!

343
00:19:36,260 --> 00:19:37,980
No cheating in the second stage!

344
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:39,960
Next is the artistic category

345
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:44,100
We will now begin judging the
artistic category of the second stage.

346
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:46,200
The time limit is 30 minutes.

347
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:46,815
Got it?

348
00:19:46,865 --> 00:19:52,720
The enemies will go all out with flashy styles, but don't be swayed by that.
Just keep attacking with the crew cut. Understand?!

349
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:56,660
Please fully display your originality.

350
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:09,960
What does
"originality" even mean? Well, it's about creativity, or a hairstyle no one else has, something like that.

351
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:14,140
Originality, what about it,
old man Shibata? Well,

352
00:20:17,820 --> 00:20:21,900
once you get going like that,
don't worry about what others think.

353
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:26,400
It's a crew cut!

354
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:28,280
We're strictly crew cuts.

355
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:32,120
What's the matter with you?

356
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:34,580
The crew cut is a tradition, you know.

357
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:37,460
Isn't originality missing from it?
Is that really okay?

358
00:20:37,460 --> 00:20:38,340
Good.

359
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:41,980
But a plain crew cut alone is just too dull,
isn't it?

360
00:20:41,980 --> 00:20:42,960
It's fine, I'm telling you.

361
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:47,000
In a flashy parade like that,
the plain one actually stands out more.

362
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,260
We only just had a meeting yesterday,
didn't we?

363
00:20:52,580 --> 00:20:53,100
Not so fast!

364
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:02,700
Ugh, aaaah, it's cheap!

365
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:07,300
Nobody's into crew cuts these days, man.
The world's looking for something new,

366
00:21:09,300 --> 00:21:09,620
Alright.

367
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:11,800
Mm.

368
00:21:14,980 --> 00:21:16,740
Whoa, that's cold!

369
00:21:16,740 --> 00:21:18,400
Just a little bit, come on.

370
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:21,520
Hey, what are you doing?

371
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:26,540
Don't move! A plain crew cut won't cut it these days!
You've gotta look at the wider world!

372
00:21:26,620 --> 00:21:29,780
Even so, what are you going to do
by shaving in a place like that?

373
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:31,680
30 seconds left.

374
00:21:36,560 --> 00:21:38,660
Time's up!

375
00:21:38,660 --> 00:21:41,260
Done!

376
00:21:41,260 --> 00:21:41,880
Alright!

377
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:51,480
No way.

378
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:55,300
Would you believe it?

379
00:21:55,300 --> 00:21:56,360
Shibata too?

380
00:21:56,360 --> 00:21:57,300
Old man

381
00:21:57,300 --> 00:21:59,620
What's so funny?

382
00:22:00,260 --> 00:22:01,220
What?

383
00:22:01,220 --> 00:22:04,640
What's with this guy?

384
00:22:40,220 --> 00:22:41,260
It's not like I dislike you or anything.

385
00:22:41,260 --> 00:22:42,800
What's with that attitude?

386
00:22:44,020 --> 00:22:46,420
I'm just clumsy, so I can't bring
myself to be openly happy about it.

387
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:48,040
Really, I'm super happy.

388
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:48,520
Is that so?

389
00:22:48,520 --> 00:22:49,360
Ryo-san

390
00:22:50,140 --> 00:22:52,360
I owe you a lot for everything you've done.

391
00:22:52,820 --> 00:22:53,460
Thanks.

392
00:22:53,920 --> 00:22:56,520
Forget that. From now on,
don't be picky about who you serve,

393
00:22:56,520 --> 00:22:58,240
and take on every customer
who walks through the door.

394
00:22:58,240 --> 00:22:59,340
The gauge went up too.

395
00:22:59,340 --> 00:23:00,880
Things are going to get
tough for the business.

396
00:23:01,520 --> 00:23:02,240
Don't worry about it.

397
00:23:02,560 --> 00:23:04,440
From now on, I'll handle the accounts.

398
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:06,280
Ryo-san.

399
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:07,820
Take off that hanten jacket.

400
00:23:07,820 --> 00:23:10,300
The lifetime free pass has been abolished.

401
00:23:10,300 --> 00:23:11,040
What?

402
00:23:11,680 --> 00:23:13,300
So that's how it is. Sorry.

403
00:23:13,300 --> 00:23:15,120
And we missed out on the prize money.

404
00:23:15,120 --> 00:23:16,900
If sorry settled everything,
we'd have no need for the police.

405
00:23:16,900 --> 00:23:18,200
There you are!

406
00:23:19,320 --> 00:23:21,620
Hey, old man,
you were on TV the other day, weren't you?

407
00:23:21,620 --> 00:23:23,220
The crew cut, you know?

408
00:23:23,620 --> 00:23:25,300
Why don't you just go ahead
and give it a quick snip for us?

409
00:23:25,780 --> 00:23:26,140
Hey!

410
00:23:26,140 --> 00:23:28,140
Right off the bat with
the casual talk You punks.

411
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:31,080
Just because you're customers
doesn't mean you can get cocky, got it?

412
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:33,200
W-who are you?

413
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:37,040
I'm telling you, repeat losers like
you had better watch how you talk.

414
00:23:38,160 --> 00:23:39,540
I'll do this to you!

415
00:23:40,780 --> 00:23:43,060
Please, anything but that. Have mercy.

416
00:23:43,060 --> 00:23:46,460
Don't mess around with this man's head!

417
00:24:08,620 --> 00:24:11,180
A mysterious feeling

418
00:24:12,820 --> 00:24:16,900
So, on the arcade guide tiles,

419
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:22,680
I tried walking only on the black parts.

420
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:28,840
Everyone was a child once,

421
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:30,940
but everyone has forgotten.

422
00:24:31,840 --> 00:24:34,980
Politicians with their
self-important faces won't do.

423
00:24:34,980 --> 00:24:38,360
and neither will the
aunties with blue eyeshadow.

424
00:24:38,360 --> 00:24:41,280
Try turning the corner.

425
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:43,860
That corner there.

426
00:24:44,920 --> 00:24:49,040
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

427
00:24:51,020 --> 00:24:53,640
Over there is Kameari,

428
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:57,020
surely Kameari is there.

429
00:24:58,360 --> 00:25:02,180
Everyone, come on over to our town!

430
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:06,900
Over there is Kameari,

431
00:25:08,500 --> 00:25:10,180
surely Kameari is there.

432
00:25:11,700 --> 00:25:15,480
Everyone, come on over to our town!

433
00:25:16,560 --> 00:25:16,960
Thank you.

434
00:25:20,100 --> 00:25:24,100
I built a one-of-a-kind
bicycle just for Lemon!

435
00:25:24,620 --> 00:25:26,200
What? It was stolen?

436
00:25:26,560 --> 00:25:30,320
I won't forgive this! You'll learn
what happens when you make me angry!

437
00:25:32,180 --> 00:25:33,600
There's not even a bicycle left

438
00:25:34,180 --> 00:25:36,080
Next time: Operation Cycle!

439
00:25:36,080 --> 00:25:36,940
Nice to meet you.

